.TH CHAOS 1 "2026-09" "chaos-toolbox" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
chaos \- small, time-boxed chaos experiments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chaos
.I experiment
.B \-\-duration
.I TIME
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs one small chaos experiment against this machine or container and
cleans up after itself: network rules are removed on exit.
.PP
Every experiment requires
.BR \-\-duration .
There is no open-ended mode, because an experiment nobody remembered to
stop is an outage.
.PP
Network experiments act on this container's network namespace. Share the
target pod's network (as a sidecar, or with
.BR "kubectl debug \-\-target" )
and grant CAP_NET_ADMIN.
.PP
Without
.B \-\-to
the network experiments degrade the whole interface, which includes
whatever is watching the experiment.
.B \-\-to
limits them to destination CIDRs, so one dependency can be degraded while
the rest of the host's traffic \(em metrics, health checks, your shell \(em
is untouched.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI cpu " \-\-duration TIME"
Burn CPU on
.I \-\-workers
workers at
.I \-\-load
percent.
.TP
.BI mem " \-\-duration TIME"
Hold
.I \-\-bytes
of memory on
.I \-\-workers
workers.
.TP
.BI io " \-\-duration TIME"
Generate disk I/O on
.I \-\-workers
workers.
.TP
.BI delay " \-\-duration TIME"
Add
.I \-\-ms
latency with
.I \-\-jitter
to the interface.
.TP
.BI loss " \-\-duration TIME"
Drop
.I \-\-pct
percent of packets.
.TP
.BI limit " \-\-duration TIME"
Shape the interface down to
.IR \-\-rate .
.TP
.BI kill " \-\-duration TIME \-\-target PATTERN"
Restart matching workloads every
.IR \-\-every ,
for the window, then stop. There is no "everything" default: the blast
radius of a typo should be one workload, not a cluster.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Common
.TP
.BI \-\-duration " TIME"
How long the experiment runs, e.g.
.BR 60s ,
.BR 5m .
Required \(em it is the safety rail.
.TP
.BI \-\-workers " N"
Worker processes (default 2).
.TP
.BI \-\-probe " URL"
Turn the experiment into an experiment
.IR report :
latency is sampled against URL before injection and again during it, and
the two sets of percentiles are printed. Without it, an experiment
proves that it ran, not what it did.
.TP
.BI \-\-report " FILE"
Write the probe's before/after percentiles to FILE as JSON.
.TP
.BI \-\-baseline " TIME"
How long to sample before injecting (default 10s).
.TP
.BI \-\-probe\-interval " SEC"
Seconds between probe samples (default 1).
.SS Resource experiments
.TP
.BI \-\-load " PCT"
CPU load percentage for
.B cpu
(default 80).
.TP
.BI \-\-bytes " SIZE"
Memory held by
.B mem
(default 256M).
.SS Network experiments
.TP
.BI \-\-ms " MS"
Added latency for
.B delay
(default 200).
.TP
.BI \-\-jitter " MS"
Jitter around
.B \-\-ms
(default 50).
.TP
.BI \-\-pct " PCT"
Packet loss percentage for
.B loss
(default 10).
.TP
.BI \-\-rate " RATE"
Bandwidth ceiling for
.B limit
(default 1mbit).
.TP
.BI \-\-dev " IFACE"
Interface to act on (default eth0).
.TP
.BI \-\-to " CIDR"
Restrict the experiment to these destination CIDRs. Repeatable, or
comma-separated. Strongly recommended: without it the whole interface
is degraded.
.SS Restart experiment
.TP
.BI \-\-target " PATTERN"
What
.B kill
restarts. Required for that experiment.
.TP
.BI \-\-every " TIME"
Interval between restarts (default 20s).
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " docker|k8s"
Where to restart. Docker mode needs the socket mounted; k8s mode needs a
kubeconfig or service account that can delete pods.
.TP
.BI \-\-namespace " NS"
Namespace for
.BR "\-\-mode k8s" .
.TP
.BI \-\-signal " SIG"
Signal to send (default SIGKILL).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print what would be restarted, and restart nothing.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the built-in help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The experiment ran and cleaned up.
.TP
.B 64
Usage error: an unknown flag, or a missing
.BR \-\-duration .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Saturate two cores for a minute, and measure what it did to an endpoint:
.PP
.RS
.B chaos cpu \-\-duration 60s \-\-load 90 \-\-probe http://localhost:8080/healthz
.RE
.PP
Add latency to one dependency only, leaving the rest of the host alone:
.PP
.RS
.B chaos delay \-\-duration 2m \-\-ms 300 \-\-to 10.0.4.0/24
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tc (8),
.BR netem (8).
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/chaos-toolbox
.UE
